  "unmapped_findings": [
    "The stacking fault energy (SFE) of this steel is 72 mJ m^-2 at room temperature and 51 mJ m^-2 at cryogenic temperature; the cryogenic SFE is still higher than the ~20–40 mJ m^-2 typically associated with twinning plasticity, but low-temperature dislocation restraint promotes deformation twinning at moderate CR strains before dislocation slip becomes predominant at 70% CR (b0044, b0047)."
  ]
}
